{
  "schema_version": "formalization-faithfulness-1",
  "role": "adjudicator",
  "task_id": "LEV-CH01-EQ-1.2-ADVECTION-CANONICAL-20260908",
  "trigger": [
    "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The target correctly expresses classical scalar specialization, but the selected passage also asserts equation satisfaction for transported concentration and hyperbolicity of the real scalar problem. Neither assertion occurs in the target. Retain not-faithful-weaker and accepted=false. Narrowing the source claim to representation equivalence would change the audit selection and cannot be inferred from the theorem name.",
      "primary_evidence": "The attached raw PDF page 23, printed page 1, contains the scalar specialization paragraph, its hyperbolicity assertion, and the sentence introducing equation (1.2) that asserts satisfaction by contaminant concentration. The elaborated target is universally quantified Iff between D002 applied to the singleton embedding and D003; neither side is asserted independently."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "D005 and D006 require precisely two slice derivatives at the selected point, without continuous derivatives, joint differentiability, or neighborhood regularity. This matches the displayed equation under a classical interpretation. It does not establish coverage of every solution concept intended by the book. That broader ambiguity remains, but it does not obstruct the representation equivalence: the theorem imposes no differentiability antecedent on q and asserts no derivative existence outside its two predicates. Separately, C04 fails for the complete selected modeling assertion because no transport premise is linked to equation satisfaction.",
      "primary_evidence": "The primary page explicitly explains the partial-derivative subscripts after equation (1.1), states no regularity class, and subsequently describes equation (1.3) using any profile function. The supplied bodies of D005 and D006 each contain existential derivative witnesses, two HasDerivAt assertions, and the balance equality. D007 and D008 concern continuity of ambient scalar multiplication, not regularity of q."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Zero and negative velocities and all real coordinates are included. Both predicates still require a spatial derivative at zero speed. For q(x,t)=|x| at x=0 and speed=0, both classical predicates are false, while their equivalence remains valid. Thus zero speed supplies no counterexample to the target's representation claim and no excluded case of the theorem's outer quantification. Whether the source also admits this stationary nonsmooth field through a reduced or weak equation is unresolved; the target supplies no such solution characterization.",
      "primary_evidence": "The primary page states no nonzero, sign, boundary, or nonnegative-time restriction. The target binds speed, x, and t as unrestricted Real values. D005 and D006 retain both HasDerivAt conjuncts independently of speed; D001 fixes the singleton matrix entry to speed, and D043 reduces its product to multiplication by that entry."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The existential witnesses are derivative values for an already supplied q, not a constructed solution. There is no prescribed-data existence, uniqueness, or well-posedness assertion in either the target or the selected equation passage. The target's classical derivative requirements are fully determined; the source's broader solution concept remains unspecified. No additional smoothness assumption or purported stronger existence result is present.",
      "primary_evidence": "The attached page gives equation (1.2) without initial or boundary data or a prescribed-data theorem. In D005 and D006, Exists binds qt and qx within each predicate. The elaborated target universally binds q before those predicates and contains no existentially quantified field or uniqueness clause."
    },
    {
      "item": "Disputed dependency D009 and task-specific effects of reused dependencies",
      "resolution": "D009 means ordinary logical equivalence and is not a defective dependency. Its placement as the entire conclusion accounts for the missing satisfaction assertion. Rechecking D005 from its supplied body confirms actual derivative witnesses and the matrix balance. D007 supplies ambient continuity only. D014–D016 and D043 give exactly one matrix component; D017, D041, D044, D063, D080, and D091 give ordinary real scaling; D064–D068 and D102 preserve coordinatewise vector operations and the singleton product topology. These declarations support scalar specialization but introduce neither physical transport nor hyperbolicity. Reuse provenance does not supply those missing claims.",
      "primary_evidence": "The complete inline inventory supplies the body of D005, the explicit type of D007, the singleton constructions D001 and D004, the row-dot-product body of D043, the real self-module construction D017, and the pointwise operations and product topology. D002 and D003 are abbreviations for D005 and D006. The complete target contains Iff and no transport or hyperbolicity predicate."
    },
    {
      "item": "C12 nonvacuity disagreement and classification consistency",
      "resolution": "C12 passes for the proposition actually stated. Fin 1 is inhabited, no impossible premises occur, and both solution predicates can hold for nonconstant fields, for example q(x,t)=(x-speed*t)^2. Their simultaneous falsity for q(x,t)=t does not make a representation equivalence improperly vacuous. It demonstrates that the equivalence supplies no solution-status assertion. The round-trip C12 failure should therefore be reassigned to conclusion completeness and outer logical scope. Universal applicability of this equivalence does not make it a stronger version of the omitted modeling claim.",
      "primary_evidence": "The explicit target fixes dimension 1 and has no antecedent assumptions. Substitution into D005 and D006 gives time derivative -2*speed*(x-speed*t), spatial derivative 2*(x-speed*t), and residual zero for the squared translated profile. For q(x,t)=t the corresponding residual is 1, so both predicates are false. The primary source asserts equation satisfaction for transported concentration."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "The target establishes equivalence of two classical pointwise predicates after singleton identification. It provides neither a premise connecting q to physical transport nor a conclusion that the transported concentration satisfies either predicate, and it contains no hyperbolicity assertion. Universal quantification over points does not turn predicate equivalence into global satisfaction. The field q(x,t)=t illustrates this logical distinction, rather than serving as a counterexample to the physical model. The complete selected source assertion is therefore not represented by the Lean proposition."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "The selected source's explicit scalar specialization, together with ordinary real calculus and the supplied definitions, supports the target's representation claim. Evaluating vector derivative witnesses at the sole Fin 1 coordinate yields scalar derivative witnesses and the equality qt+speed*qx=0. Conversely, embedding scalar witnesses as singleton vectors preserves the slice derivatives and gives the matrix balance. These transformations work without assuming that either predicate holds beforehand, so the equivalence applies to arbitrary q, including nondifferentiable cases where both predicates are false. The source's unspecified broader solution concept does not require every source solution to satisfy these classical predicates, because the target asserts only their equivalence."
    }
  },
  "classification": "not-faithful-weaker",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The selected primary-source page does not specify whether its intended solutions are exclusively classical or also include nonsmooth solutions through another formulation. In particular, it does not settle the solution-status interpretation of nonsmooth stationary profiles at zero velocity. This uncertainty does not change either implication verdict for the representation theorem actually stated."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "modeling-assertion-omitted",
      "evidence": "The primary page asserts that concentration or density in the stated constant-velocity transport setting satisfies equation (1.2). The elaborated Lean target asserts only Iff between two solution predicates for arbitrary q.",
      "impact": "The target cannot recover the selected connection between physical transport and satisfaction of the PDE."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "hyperbolicity-conclusion-omitted",
      "evidence": "The selected scalar-specialization paragraph states hyperbolicity for real scalar A. No hyperbolicity property occurs in the target or its defining predicates.",
      "impact": "The target omits a conclusion of the selected passage; typing the coefficient as Real does not itself express that conclusion."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "correct-nonvacuous-classical-specialization",
      "evidence": "D001–D006, D017, D042, D043, and the singleton function structures preserve the real scalar field, coordinate order, actual partial derivatives, constant coefficient, plus sign, and exact zero balance. Nonconstant translated polynomial profiles satisfy both predicates.",
      "impact": "The rejection concerns incomplete representation of the selected source claim, not an incorrect operator, empty domain, or unsupported stronger smoothness requirement."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "I independently inspected the attached primary-source page and the supplied proof-free declarations, dependency inventory, reuse records, blind dossier and translation, and both judgments. The decisive distinction is between identifying two equation predicates and asserting equation satisfaction in the source's modeling setting. Singleton projection and embedding establish both directions of the internal equivalence, including derivative existence, while leaving the physical and hyperbolicity assertions absent. The regularity ambiguity is preserved without treating it as a counterexample to that equivalence. The no/yes implication pair consistently yields not-faithful-weaker. No tools were used, no files were written, and no source or rendering hashes were independently recomputed."
}
